 "isa": "arm64",
 "metric": "user CPU time differential t(16) - t(10) of C binary-trees, native timing inside lang-lab-wasm:c, pinned to one CPU, every (variant, size) pair in random order per repetition",
 "ratioMeaning": "paired per repetition: variant differential / clang (toClang) or / wasmtime default (toWasmtimeDefault); lower is better",
 "description": "binary-trees runs 1.02x native clang's instructions on wasmtime 50 but more of its time. The knobs batch varies wasmtime's memory and code-generation configuration and replaces malloc/free with a free list (fl-*); the patch batch rewrites the register save and restore code of chosen functions in the precompiled module from Cranelift's chained stack-pointer updates to one stack adjustment with the same instruction count (repatch.py; a timing probe, not a fix: .eh_frame is not updated).",
 "caveats": [
  "absolute milliseconds are comparable only within a batch (host load drifted); the ratios are paired",
  "the memory knobs that raise time (signals-based-traps=n, memory-reservation/guard-size 0) switch wasmtime to explicit bounds checks, which add instructions: they are not a memory-system measurement"
 ],
